{"title":"2020 OIM Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> be an integer. A sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e8ec52ecfddf0945f566969f719a49b1cf31fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = (a_1, a_2, \\cdots , a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers is \"<i>Limeña</i>\" (from Lima, Perú) if \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/8076851153da59ac38cadc3d80430249a908f382.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[gcd \\left\\{  a_i - a_j | a_i &gt; a_j, 1 \\le i, j \\le n\\right\\} = 1\\]\" width=\"294\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>An \"<i>operation</i>\" consists of choosing two elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0fbe5ec5c23c03ef3fbffef0b3974077988273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> of a sequence, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbae26633ee7a308593b4dc810bbc8cb88e764f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ne l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />,\nand replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0fbe5ec5c23c03ef3fbffef0b3974077988273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/5030ef0ab89ed66b22c808da40acb17535a067b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;_l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"17\" height=\"20\" />  Show that, given a collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b063495d0243e7bc52c3a7f231362bdc4a03775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> <i>Limeñan</i> sequences, each formed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers numbers, there are two of them, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, such that it is possible to transform <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> by a finite number of operations.\n<b>Clarification:</b> If all the elements of a sequence are equal, then that sequence is not <i>Limeña</i>.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013200\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 91/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2692/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.115      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    6.115      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26240:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013200 and revision id 208203. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}